# Commit Message Standards

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

**Format:** `<type>([optional scope]): <description>`

## Allowed Commit Types

- `feature` — new capability
- `fix` — bug fix
- `docs` — documentation only (e.g. README, `.cursor/rules/`, `PLAN.md`)
- `style` — formatting changes that do not affect logic
- `refactor` — neither fix nor feature
- `perf` — performance improvement
- `test` — add or correct tests
- `chore` — tooling, dependencies, build scripts

## Scopes

Prefer domain scopes: `lunar-dates`, `ics`, `App`, `hooks`, `ui`.

## Breaking Changes

Use `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the footer, or `!` after the type/scope (e.g. `feature!:`).

## Examples

- `feature(ics): add all-day lunar milestone calendar export`
- `fix(lunar-dates): use UTC date parts for ICS DATE values`
- `test(lunar-dates): cover leap-month 初一 notifications`
- `docs: clarify cursor rules and file sizing caps`
